  ))}

  <h2>How Ophis implements this</h2>
  <p>
    Ophis adds a natural-language intent layer (describe the trade, the parser fills the order), a
    public <a href="https://docs.ophis.fi/ai-agents">MCP server</a> so autonomous agents can trade
    with their own keys, and the <a href="https://github.com/ophis-fi/ophis/tree/main/packages/sdk">@ophis/sdk</a>
    safety helpers for building bounded orders. Fees are on the
    <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a>, the chain list on
    <a href="/supported-chains/">supported chains</a>, and the custody and audit detail on the
    <a href="/security/">security page</a>. For the MEV mechanics in depth, read
    <a href="/learn/mev-protected-swaps/">MEV-protected swaps, explained</a>.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
